{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R4ZGkLh8YonhLgUyvp7NRE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd063-timeout\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/timeout: Run a Command with a Time Limit\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Build scripts, CI pipelines, and system administration tools use timeout to run a command\n6\t  with a time limit and kill it if it does not complete. The macOS BSD system has no built-in\n7\t  timeout command. GNU timeout from coreutils provides duration parsing, signal selection,\n8\t  and kill-after escalation. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n9\t  binary (gtimeout, installed by coreutils) in exit codes and signal behavior, verified by\n10\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Run a command and kill it if it exceeds a specified duration.\n14\t  - G2: Support configurable signal selection and kill-after escalation.\n15\t  - G3: Support duration suffixes (s, m, h, d) and fractional values.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Core timeout behavior\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: \"Must run COMMAND with optional ARGS and kill it with SIGTERM if it does not exit within DURATION seconds.\"\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Must support fractional durations (e.g., timeout 0.5 command).\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: Must support suffix multipliers s (seconds, default), m (minutes), h (hours), d (days).\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: \"When DURATION is 0, must not impose a time limit (the command runs indefinitely).\"\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Signal selection and kill-after\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"-s SIGNAL or --signal=SIGNAL must send the specified signal instead of SIGTERM. Must accept signal names (e.g., KILL, HUP) and numeric signal values.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: \"-k DURATION or --kill-after=DURATION must send SIGKILL if the command is still running DURATION seconds after the initial signal.\"\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: \"--foreground must not create a separate process group, allowing the command to use the terminal.\"\n39\t      - R2.4:\n40\t          text: \"--preserve-status must exit with the same status as the command, even on timeout, instead of the timeout-specific exit code 124.\"\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Exit codes\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: \"When the command exits before the timeout, must exit with the command's exit status.\"\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: \"When the command is killed due to timeout, must exit 124 (unless --preserve-status is given).\"\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: \"When the command is killed by a signal not sent by timeout, must exit 128+signum.\"\n51\t      - R3.4:\n52\t          text: \"When the timeout command itself fails (invalid arguments, command not found), must exit 125 for internal error or 126/127 for command execution failure.\"\n53\t\n54\t  R4:\n55\t    title: Differential testing\n56\t    items:\n57\t      - R4.1:\n58\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n59\t      - R4.2:\n60\t          text: \"Tests must cover: command completes before timeout (exit with command status), command exceeds timeout (exit 124), duration 0 (no limit), -s with named and numeric signals, -k kill-after escalation, --preserve-status, and error cases (no args, invalid duration, command not found).\"\n61\t      - R4.3:\n62\t          text: \"Tests must use fast commands (true, false, sleep 0) and short durations to avoid slow test execution.\"\n63\t      - R4.4:\n64\t          text: \"Tests must verify that the timed-out process is actually killed and does not remain as an orphan.\"\n65\t\n66\tnon_goals:\n67\t  - cmd/timeout does not implement --verbose or any diagnostic output beyond error messages.\n68\t  - cmd/timeout does not implement platform-specific process group management beyond what Go's os/exec provides with SysProcAttr.Setpgid.\n69\t\n70\tacceptance_criteria:\n71\t  - id: AC1\n72\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout 10 true exits 0, matching gtimeout.\"\n73\t    traces:\n74\t      - R1.1\n75\t      - R3.1\n76\t  - id: AC2\n77\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout 0.01 sleep 10 exits 124, matching gtimeout.\"\n78\t    traces:\n79\t      - R1.1\n80\t      - R1.2\n81\t      - R3.2\n82\t  - id: AC3\n83\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout 0 sleep 0 exits 0 (no time limit), matching gtimeout.\"\n84\t    traces:\n85\t      - R1.4\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t  - id: AC4\n88\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout -s KILL 0.01 sleep 10 sends SIGKILL and exits 137, matching gtimeout.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R2.1\n91\t      - R3.3\n92\t  - id: AC5\n93\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtimeout passes for all cases listed in R4.2.\"\n94\t    traces:\n95\t      - R4.1\n96\t      - R4.2\n97\t      - R4.3\n98\t      - R4.4\n99\t  - id: AC6\n100\t    criterion: \"cmd/timeout compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R1.1\n103\t      - R1.2\n104\t      - R1.3\n105\t      - R1.4\n106\t      - R2.1\n107\t      - R2.2\n108\t      - R2.3\n109\t      - R2.4\n110\t      - R3.1\n111\t      - R3.2\n112\t      - R3.3\n113\t      - R3.4\n114\t      - R4.1\n115\t      - R4.2\n116\t      - R4.3\n117\t      - R4.4\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0257407e-6ee4-42e2-a7f2-a490be4c0a8c","uuid":"9a8447d6-325e-44e6-8550-76cad4374a7e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T15:06:35.670Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5424/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd063-timeout.yaml","content":"id: srd063-timeout\ntitle: \"cmd/timeout: Run a Command with a Time Limit\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Build scripts, CI pipelines, and system administration tools use timeout to run a command\n  with a time limit and kill it if it does not complete. The macOS BSD system has no built-in\n  timeout command. GNU timeout from coreutils provides duration parsing, signal selection,\n  and kill-after escalation. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (gtimeout, installed by coreutils) in exit codes and signal behavior, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Run a command and kill it if it exceeds a specified duration.\n  - G2: Support configurable signal selection and kill-after escalation.\n  - G3: Support duration suffixes (s, m, h, d) and fractional values.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Core timeout behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"Must run COMMAND with optional ARGS and kill it with SIGTERM if it does not exit within DURATION seconds.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must support fractional durations (e.g., timeout 0.5 command).\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must support suffix multipliers s (seconds, default), m (minutes), h (hours), d (days).\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"When DURATION is 0, must not impose a time limit (the command runs indefinitely).\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Signal selection and kill-after\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-s SIGNAL or --signal=SIGNAL must send the specified signal instead of SIGTERM. Must accept signal names (e.g., KILL, HUP) and numeric signal values.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-k DURATION or --kill-after=DURATION must send SIGKILL if the command is still running DURATION seconds after the initial signal.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"--foreground must not create a separate process group, allowing the command to use the terminal.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"--preserve-status must exit with the same status as the command, even on timeout, instead of the timeout-specific exit code 124.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"When the command exits before the timeout, must exit with the command's exit status.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"When the command is killed due to timeout, must exit 124 (unless --preserve-status is given).\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"When the command is killed by a signal not sent by timeout, must exit 128+signum.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"When the timeout command itself fails (invalid arguments, command not found), must exit 125 for internal error or 126/127 for command execution failure.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: command completes before timeout (exit with command status), command exceeds timeout (exit 124), duration 0 (no limit), -s with named and numeric signals, -k kill-after escalation, --preserve-status, and error cases (no args, invalid duration, command not found).\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Tests must use fast commands (true, false, sleep 0) and short durations to avoid slow test execution.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Tests must verify that the timed-out process is actually killed and does not remain as an orphan.\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/timeout does not implement --verbose or any diagnostic output beyond error messages.\n  - cmd/timeout does not implement platform-specific process group management beyond what Go's os/exec provides with SysProcAttr.Setpgid.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout 10 true exits 0, matching gtimeout.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout 0.01 sleep 10 exits 124, matching gtimeout.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout 0 sleep 0 exits 0 (no time limit), matching gtimeout.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.4\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/timeout -s KILL 0.01 sleep 10 sends SIGKILL and exits 137, matching gtimeout.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtimeout passes for all cases listed in R4.2.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/timeout compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
