{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's task is to implement srd063 requirements R2.1-R2.4 for `cmd/timeout`, extending the existing timeout utility with signal selection, kill-after escalation, foreground mode, and preserve-status functionality. This is task #5424 in a cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline (stitch phase). The task explicitly states: preserve existing R1.1-R1.4 implementation, extend don't rewrite. All changes must be verified by differential testing against `gtimeout` (GNU timeout from Homebrew).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (gtimeout)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests and testutils.BuildBinary for test harness\n   - SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Process group management via syscall.SysProcAttr{Setpgid: true}\n   - GNU-style flag parsing for timeout: `[OPTIONS] DURATION COMMAND [ARG...]`\n   - Signal name/number parsing (KILL, HUP, TERM, numeric values)\n   - Kill-after escalation: secondary SIGKILL timer after initial signal\n   - Exit codes: 0 (success), 124 (timeout), 125 (internal error), 126/127 (exec failure), 128+signum (signal)\n   - 40-line function limit (E8), 500-line file limit (E9)\n   - Write all code before building/testing (go_style_constitution implementation_strategy)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd063-timeout.yaml** (SRD - read in full)\n     - Defines R2.1: `-s SIGNAL` / `--signal=SIGNAL` for signal selection (names and numeric)\n     - Defines R2.2: `-k DURATION` / `--kill-after=DURATION` for SIGKILL escalation\n     - Defines R2.3: `--foreground` to skip process group creation\n     - Defines R2.4: `--preserve-status` to exit with command's status instead of 124\n     - Non-goals: no --verbose, no platform-specific process group beyond SysProcAttr.Setpgid\n\n   - **cmd/timeout/main.go** (existing implementation - 133 lines)\n     - Current implementation has no flag parsing, uses raw os.Args positional args\n     - `main()`: installs SIGPIPE handler, parses duration from args[0], runs command with process group, sets timer for SIGTERM, handles exit codes\n     - `parseDuration(s string)`: parses float with s/m/h/d suffix multipliers\n     - `isNotFound(err error)`: checks if error is command-not-found\n     - Uses `syscall.Kill(-cmd.Process.Pid, syscall.SIGTERM)` for process group kill\n     - Sets `cmd.SysProcAttr = &syscall.SysProcAttr{Setpgid: true}` always\n     - Full code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"os/exec\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"time\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         if len(args) < 2 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: missing operand\\nTry 'timeout --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(125)\n         }\n         duration, err := parseDuration(args[0])\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: invalid time interval %q\\n\", args[0])\n             os.Exit(125)\n         }\n         cmdArgs := args[1:]\n         cmd := exec.Command(cmdArgs[0], cmdArgs[1:]...)\n         cmd.Stdin = os.Stdin\n         cmd.Stdout = os.Stdout\n         cmd.Stderr = os.Stderr\n         cmd.SysProcAttr = &syscall.SysProcAttr{Setpgid: true}\n         if err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n             if isNotFound(err) {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: failed to run command %q: %v\\n\", cmdArgs[0], err)\n                 os.Exit(127)\n             }\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: failed to run command %q: %v\\n\", cmdArgs[0], err)\n             os.Exit(126)\n         }\n         timedOut := false\n         var timer *time.Timer\n         if duration > 0 {\n             timer = time.AfterFunc(duration, func() {\n                 timedOut = true\n                 _ = syscall.Kill(-cmd.Process.Pid, syscall.SIGTERM)\n             })\n         }\n         waitErr := cmd.Wait()\n         if timer != nil { timer.Stop() }\n         if waitErr == nil { os.Exit(0) }\n         exitErr, ok := waitErr.(*exec.ExitError)\n         if !ok {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: %v\\n\", waitErr)\n             os.Exit(125)\n         }\n         status, ok := exitErr.Sys().(syscall.WaitStatus)\n         if !ok { os.Exit(exitErr.ExitCode()) }\n         if status.Signaled() {\n             signum := int(status.Signal())\n             if timedOut && status.Signal() == syscall.SIGTERM {\n                 os.Exit(124)\n             }\n             os.Exit(128 + signum)\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitErr.ExitCode())\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go** (existing tests - 92 lines)\n     - Has 12 test cases covering R1.1-R1.4\n     - Uses `clearStderr` normalizer to ignore stderr differences\n     - Tests: command_completes_before_timeout, command_fails_before_timeout, command_exceeds_timeout, fractional_duration, suffix_seconds, suffix_minutes, duration_zero_no_limit, duration_zero_suffix_no_limit, no_args, missing_command, command_not_found, invalid_duration\n     - Full code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"os/exec\"\n         \"testing\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n     )\n     var clearStderr testutils.NormalizeFunc = func(b []byte) []byte { return nil }\n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gtimeout\")\n         if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n             {Name: \"command_completes_before_timeout\", Args: []string{\"10\", \"true\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n             {Name: \"command_fails_before_timeout\", Args: []string{\"10\", \"false\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n             {Name: \"command_exceeds_timeout\", Args: []string{\"0.01\", \"sleep\", \"10\"}, ExitCode: 124},\n             {Name: \"fractional_duration\", Args: []string{\"0.5\", \"true\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n             {Name: \"suffix_seconds\", Args: []string{\"10s\", \"true\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n             {Name: \"suffix_minutes\", Args: []string{\"1m\", \"true\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n             {Name: \"duration_zero_no_limit\", Args: []string{\"0\", \"true\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n             {Name: \"duration_zero_suffix_no_limit\", Args: []string{\"0s\", \"true\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n             {Name: \"no_args\", Args: []string{}, ExitCode: 125, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{clearStderr}},\n             {Name: \"missing_command\", Args: []string{\"10\"}, ExitCode: 125, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{clearStderr}},\n             {Name: \"command_not_found\", Args: []string{\"10\", \"nonexistent_command_xyz_123\"}, ExitCode: 127, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{clearStderr}},\n             {Name: \"invalid_duration\", Args: []string{\"abc\", \"true\"}, ExitCode: 125, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{clearStderr}},\n         }\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Files were only read, no code changes attempted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the existing implementation uses raw os.Args without flag parsing, so adding -s, -k, --foreground, --preserve-status requires implementing GNU-style option parsing (options before positional DURATION and COMMAND args)\n   - Need to handle signal name-to-number mapping (KILL→9, HUP→1, TERM→15, etc.)\n   - Kill-after requires a second timer that sends SIGKILL after the initial signal's duration\n   - Foreground mode requires conditionally setting Setpgid and using process kill vs process group kill\n   - Preserve-status changes exit code from 124 to 128+signum on timeout\n   - The timedOut check for exit 124 needs to account for the custom signal (not just SIGTERM)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial message is the full task prompt with massive project context, SRD references, execution constitution, go style constitution, and specific task description for implementing srd063 R2.1-R2.4 for cmd/timeout.\n   - No additional user messages with feedback yet - only the initial task.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement flag parsing in cmd/timeout/main.go for: -s/--signal, -k/--kill-after, --foreground, --preserve-status\n   - Implement signal name/number parsing function\n   - Implement kill-after SIGKILL escalation timer\n   - Implement foreground mode (skip Setpgid, use direct process kill instead of process group kill)\n   - Implement preserve-status exit code logic\n   - Add differential tests for all R2.1-R2.4 scenarios to cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/timeout ./cmd/timeout/`\n   - Verify: `go vet ./cmd/timeout/...`\n   - Verify: `go test ./cmd/timeout/... -count=1`\n   - Ensure existing R1.1-R1.4 tests still pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, timeout_test.go) and was about to begin implementing the R2.1-R2.4 requirements. No code changes have been made yet. The implementation plan involves:\n   - Adding GNU-style flag parsing to main.go to handle `-s SIGNAL`, `-k DURATION`, `--signal=SIGNAL`, `--kill-after=DURATION`, `--foreground`, `--preserve-status` before the positional DURATION and COMMAND args\n   - Adding a `parseSignal(s string)` function to convert signal names/numbers to syscall.Signal\n   - Modifying the timer callback to use the configured signal instead of hardcoded SIGTERM\n   - Adding a kill-after timer that sends SIGKILL\n   - Conditionally setting Setpgid based on --foreground\n   - Modifying exit code logic for --preserve-status\n   - Adding ~8-10 new test cases for signal selection, kill-after, foreground, and preserve-status\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the complete updated cmd/timeout/main.go with all R2.1-R2.4 functionality (flag parsing, signal selection, kill-after, foreground, preserve-status), then write the updated cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go with new differential tests, then build and test.\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd063 R2.1 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd063 R2.2 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd063 R2.3 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd063 R2.4 per the SRD specification\" with design decision D1: \"Preserve existing R1.1-R1.4 implementation -- extend, do not rewrite.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5424/0257407e-6ee4-42e2-a7f2-a490be4c0a8c.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0257407e-6ee4-42e2-a7f2-a490be4c0a8c","uuid":"01f12241-b6f3-4a09-97f5-7c3e93de8a8c","timestamp":"2026-05-21T15:07:38.411Z","isSynthetic":true}
