erminators (`--`)\n\n### 2. DiffTest Struct Fields\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5424/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 46-55):\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string\n    Args          []string\n    Stdin         []byte\n    Env           []string\n    WorkDir       string\n    ExitCode      int\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n**Field details:**\n- `Name`: Identifies the subtest (used with `t.Run`)\n- `Args`: Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n- `Stdin`: Raw stdin bytes (`nil` = EOF immediately; empty slice `[]byte{}` = open stdin immediately closed)\n- `Env`: KEY=VALUE pairs merged into inherited environment (LC_ALL=C applied by default as override)\n- `WorkDir`: Working directory (defaults to `t.TempDir()` if empty)\n- `ExitCode`: Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- `Normalize`: Slice of `NormalizeFunc` applied in order to both stdout and stderr before comparison\n- `ExpectedFiles`: Map of relative file paths to expected contents for post-execution validation\n\nAdditional feature: `TimestampNormalizer` is a built-in normalizer for common timestamp patterns.\n\n### 3. cmd/kill Status\n\n**Does NOT exist.** The cmd/ directory contains 42 utilities but `kill` is not among them. The available signal-handling utilities in the repository do not include a `kill` command implementation.\n\nThe closest signal-related code in the repository would be in the `timeout` command (which handles signals) or the general signal handling in `pkg/sys`, but there's no dedicated signal parsing module like would be found in a `kill` implementation."}],"totalDurationMs":22900,"totalTokens":34270,"totalToolUseCount":8,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2403,"cache_read_input_tokens":30992,"output_tokens":869,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{