{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015iG3imaKsBnDf3vtt5H4CB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test framework uses `exitErr.ExitCode()` which returns -1 for signal-killed processes. It compares this between the Go and reference binaries. So when gtimeout dies by SIGKILL (exit -1), our binary needs to also die by SIGKILL (exit -1) to match.\n\nThe fix: When sending SIGKILL as the initial timeout signal, also kill ourselves to match GNU behavior. For kill-after SIGKILL escalation, don't kill ourselves (gtimeout exits 124 in that case).\n\nLet me update the timer callback in main.go. \n\nModifying the timer callback...\n\nActually, I'm realizing there's a race condition here—if we send SIGKILL to ourselves, we die before the killTimer variable even gets set, so the killAfter logic never runs. But that's acceptable because if we're already sending SIGKILL as the initial signal, the child process is already terminated anyway. Now looking at how the ExitCode field in DiffTest is actually used in the comparison logic—it's checking whether the exit codes match between our implementation and the reference implementation. I'm realizing the test only compares the exit codes from the actual binary runs, not from the ExitCode field in the test case—that's just for documentation. Since the reference binary (gtimeout) exits with -1 and our binary exits with 124, the comparison fails. If I fix our implementation to also die by SIGKILL and return -1, the test should pass. Let me check if there's any other validation logic that uses the ExitCode field...\n\nno, it's only `compareOutputs` and `checkExpectedFiles`. So my plan is to update the timer callback to send SIGKILL to ourselves when needed, and then update the test expectations to reflect -1 for SIGKILL cases.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4909,"cache_read_input_tokens":41444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4909},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0257407e-6ee4-42e2-a7f2-a490be4c0a8c","uuid":"d5a21d99-7717-47c9-a88e-11a4e5dd9a03"}
